WEBVTT

00:00:09,680 --> 00:00:15,640
Does the Dutch test include that as well as adrenal hormones?

00:00:16,160 --> 00:00:21,400
So the Dutch test only includes cortisol levels and DHEA.

00:00:23,080 --> 00:00:30,520
And it gives you a cortisol rhythm. So your cortisol is released in a rhythm

00:00:31,600 --> 00:00:34,200
as well as many of your hormones are.

00:00:35,160 --> 00:00:41,440
And you have to make sure you do it on a day that is you're not under a lot of stress or

00:00:41,960 --> 00:00:43,960
kind of invalidates it.

00:00:43,960 --> 00:00:46,760
But it's going to give you the cortisol rhythm through the day.

00:00:46,760 --> 00:00:51,800
You're taking a test through, you know, four different tests through the day to get the cortisol rhythm.

00:00:52,760 --> 00:00:56,840
That could be a beneficial test, but that's really measuring just the needles.

00:00:56,840 --> 00:01:02,520
So that's going to measure what that will tell you is if your rhythm is still good,

00:01:02,520 --> 00:01:06,280
you still have a nice rhythm, but everything is suppressed.

00:01:06,280 --> 00:01:08,280
That means you have adrenal fatigue.

00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:14,520
If you're rid of, if everything is high, then you have an excess cortisol output

00:01:15,080 --> 00:01:18,440
and just excess chronic stress.

00:01:19,160 --> 00:01:24,840
Or if it's just flatline, it means you have complete adrenal, adrenal, just

00:01:26,680 --> 00:01:32,200
complete adrenal fatigue or what's it called, just complete adrenal waste that we

00:01:32,280 --> 00:01:35,160
really need to get into support of your adrenal glands.

00:01:35,160 --> 00:01:39,480
So there's benefit in doing a cortisol rhythm test.

00:01:39,480 --> 00:01:41,160
I think there's benefits to that.

